WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.660
graphed a second notochord against the side of a chick neural tube.

2
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:10.040
The neural cells beside it start to behave like floor plate.

3
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:11.860
The tube gains a second bottom.

4
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.460
So how does a cell in the wall know how far it sits from the bottom?

5
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.920
The answer is a signal called Sonic hedgehog.

6
00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:23.913
The floor plate and the notochord both make Sonic hedgehog.

7
00:00:24.433 --> 00:00:27.013
It spreads up the wall and falls off with distance.

8
00:00:27.653 --> 00:00:31.413
A signal that spreads from a source and gives different instructions at different

9
00:00:31.413 --> 00:00:33.573
concentrations is called a morphogen.

10
00:00:34.553 --> 00:00:36.433
Cells low in the wall receive a lot.

11
00:00:37.153 --> 00:00:38.853
Cells high in the wall receive little.

12
00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:42.487
Each cell answers with transcription factors.

13
00:00:43.227 --> 00:00:47.427
Class 1 factors are repressed by Sonic hedgehog, so they are lost where the signal

14
00:00:47.427 --> 00:00:52.207
is high. Class 2 factors need the signal, so they appear where it is high.

15
00:00:52.987 --> 00:00:56.487
Pack 7 is switched off by low levels, so it marks the dorsal half.

16
00:00:57.167 --> 00:01:01.407
NKX 2 .2 needs high levels, and it sits next to the floor plate.

17
00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.970
But cells read more than the level.

18
00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:09.310
Sonic hedgehog switches on its own receptor, patched one, so cells grow less

19
00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:10.870
sensitive and signaling fades.

20
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.950
A higher dose keeps signaling going longer.

21
00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:19.090
At a fixed dose, longer exposure gives progressively more ventral identities.

22
00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:24.290
In this model, a cell's identity tracks something like the total signaling it has

23
00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:25.290
received.

24
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:28.903
A smooth slope should give a blur, yet the borders are sharp.

25
00:01:29.503 --> 00:01:32.043
Factors on either side of a border repress each other.

26
00:01:32.743 --> 00:01:38.123
PAC -6 and NKX 2 .2 do this where the motor neuron domain meets the domain below.

27
00:01:38.743 --> 00:01:41.743
Such factors can form a switch with two stable states.

28
00:01:42.303 --> 00:01:45.163
A border cell settles, but a changed signal can shift it.

29
00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:48.867
The result is five ventral stripes of progenitors.

30
00:01:49.447 --> 00:01:55.347
From top to bottom they are p0, p1, p2, pMN and p3.

31
00:01:55.987 --> 00:02:02.547
They make V0, V1 and V2 interneurons, motor neurons, and V3 neurons.

32
00:02:03.307 --> 00:02:08.907
Keep this rule. A source makes a slope, cells read its level and its duration, and

33
00:02:08.907 --> 00:02:11.007
cross -repression sharpens it into domains.
